    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0245" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-09T14:00:00+08:00">April 9, 1949—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 11—4:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 204. In April 8 meeting Canton Central Executive Committee Kuomintang
                    members present voted full support for Li Tsung-jen. Question of return
                    Generalissimo to lead opposition to Communists was not raised. Resolution passed
                    that peace negotiations should end when and if Communists cross Yangtze.
                    Participation in coalition with Communists was rejected and territorial
                    settlement with Yangtze as dividing line was approved. Premier returned to
                    Nanking to report above to Acting President.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 184, Shanghai 134.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
